From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Johnson <105193579+Johnson-Anthony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] firmware: arm_scmi: perf: no turbo OPPs without a
 sustained frequency

scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add() flags every OPP above the domain's sustained
frequency as turbo. On the Surface Laptop 7 (X1E80100, SCMI perf v4.0,
level indexing) the CPUCP firmware reports sustained_freq_khz = 0 and
sustained_perf_level = 0 for NCC1 and NCC2. NCC0 reports 3417600 kHz,
level 12. So all 13 OPPs of domains 1 and 2 become turbo, and
dev_pm_opp_init_cpufreq_table() marks every entry CPUFREQ_BOOST_FREQ.

scmi_cpufreq_init() then succeeds for CPU4/CPU8. But
cpufreq_table_validate_and_sort() -> cpufreq_frequency_table_cpuinfo()
skips every boost entry, because the new policy's boost_enabled is
still false at that point even when global boost is on. It finds no
frequency, returns -EINVAL, and cpufreq_online() drops the policy with
only pr_debug output. Clusters 1 and 2 never get a policy or an energy
model, and they stay at whatever level the boot firmware left them.

A zero sustained frequency gives no turbo threshold, so mark no OPPs
turbo in that case. The mult_factor code already treats zero as "not
provided".

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
index 4583d02be..5c23a5b79 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
@@ -879,8 +879,14 @@ static int scmi_dvfs_device_opps_add(const struct scmi_protocol_handle *ph,
 		else
 			freq = dom->opp[idx].indicative_freq * dom->mult_factor;
 
-		/* All OPPs above the sustained frequency are treated as turbo */
-		data.turbo = freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
+		/*
+		 * All OPPs above the sustained frequency are treated as turbo.
+		 * A domain that reports no sustained frequency has none: marking
+		 * every OPP turbo leaves cpufreq no usable frequency with boost
+		 * off, so the policy is never created.
+		 */
+		data.turbo = dom->sustained_freq_khz &&
+			     freq > dom->sustained_freq_khz * 1000UL;
 
 		data.level = dom->opp[idx].perf;
 		data.freq = freq;
